<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A plot in Kitengela was bought for Ksh <m>{1\,500\,000}</m>. Its value appreciates at <m>{9}\%</m> a year.</p><p>(a) Find its value after <m>{4}</m> years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the appreciation over the <m>{4}</m> years.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The value is multiplied by the same number, <m>1 + \frac{ {9} }{100} = {1.09}</m>, every year.</p><p>(a) <m>V = {1\,500\,000} \times {1.09}^{ {4} } = {2\,117\,372.42}</m>, so the value is Ksh <m>{2\,117\,372}</m> to the nearest shilling.</p><p>(b) Appreciation <m>= V - P = {2\,117\,372.42} - {1\,500\,000} = {617\,372.42}</m>, about Ksh <m>{617\,372}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>2117372</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>617372</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>